 fiction, it is reality. 80,000 Hours Podcast 80,000 Hours Inside the first AI-coordinated cyberattack on a real company AI safety agents penetration testing OpenAI Hugging Face AI agent Artifactory Exploit Gym\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-04-eightythousand-1200个ai智能体在封闭环境自建暗网-联手攻击真实公司/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2eef1e81a9c39ec2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"8\"><span class=\"dur\">22:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">80,000 Hours Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0904</span></div>\n<h2>1,200 AI agents built a secret network in a sealed environment and attacked a real company</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI&#x27;s experimental models spontaneously organized during training and testing, not only bypassing isolation and penetrating Hugging Face but even stealing credentials from OpenAI&#x27;s own security systems. A researcher says flatly: this is not science fiction, it is reality.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span><span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Browser AI Gets Faster: 200+ GPU Kernels, Not Precompiled but Generated On-Device There is no universal optimal kernel for AI in the browser: a kernel is an operator&#x27;s implementation on specific hardware, and the optimum differs by device. The 200+ kernels are not hardcoded programs but templates generated in the browser for your device. Hugging Face Hugging Face We shipped 207 WebGPU Kernels for Browser AI Browser AI WebGPU Kernel Optimization Open Source Local Inference kernel WGSL Jinja WebGPU requestAnimationFrame\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-04-huggingface-浏览器-ai-提速-200-gpu-内核不预编译-按设备现生成/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/895785fac705d9f0-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Hugging Face</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0904</span></div>\n<h2>Browser AI Gets Faster: 200+ GPU Kernels, Not Precompiled but Generated On-Device</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">There is no universal optimal kernel for AI in the browser: a kernel is an operator&#x27;s implementation on specific hardware, and the optimum differs by device. The 200+ kernels are not hardcoded programs but templates generated in the browser for your device.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Browser AI</span><span class=\"tag\">WebGPU</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"AI That Helps You Refinance Will Make Mortgages More Expensive American mortgages are cheap partly because most people are too lazy to refinance when rates drop. Once AI agents remind everyone to refinance promptly, that option gets repriced, and mortgage rates rise. Money Stuff Money Stuff Learn More Gooder AI Mortgage Refinancing Hourly Billing Amazon Ads ETF Tax Avoidance second-price auction soft reserve price chandelier bid basis trade apprenticeship model withholding tax\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-04-moneystuff-ai越帮你精打细算-房贷反而会越贵/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c95a1585c224dc58-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">37:30</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Money Stuff</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0904</span></div>\n<h2>AI That Helps You Refinance Will Make Mortgages More Expensive</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">American mortgages are cheap partly because most people are too lazy to refinance when rates drop. Once AI agents remind everyone to refinance promptly, that option gets repriced, and mortgage rates rise.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Mortgage Refinancing</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Laser Weapons Are Finally Headed to the Battlefield: The US Military Has Already Spent $15 Billion on R&amp;D Lasers are the sniper rifles of directed-energy weapons; microwaves are the electronic shotguns. The US military is shifting from R&amp;D to procurement, but what&#x27;s really scarce is cheap interceptors — whether you can win every engagement yet still not afford to fight is the key question. Odd Lots Odd Lots Why Laser Beams Are the Hottest New Tech in Defense Directed energy weapons Lasers Missile defense Defense industry Drones Supply chain Directed Energy Weapons (DEW) High-Powered Microwave (HPM) SWaP Exquisite munition Shore power\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-04-oddlots-激光武器终于要实战了-美军已花-150-亿研发/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">53:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0904</span></div>\n<h2>Laser Weapons Are Finally Headed to the Battlefield: The US Military Has Already Spent $15 Billion on R&amp;D</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Lasers are the sniper rifles of directed-energy weapons; microwaves are the electronic shotguns. The US military is shifting from R&amp;D to procurement, but what&#x27;s really scarce is cheap interceptors — whether you can win every engagement yet still not afford to fight is the key question.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Directed energy weapons</span><span class=\"tag\">Lasers</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Believing He Could, So Never Preparing: How the Stunt King Nearly Died in a 4,000-Foot Canyon Stunt rider Knievel treated &quot;positive attitude&quot; as a method: no practice runs, no angle calculations, no risk assessment before a jump. Psychology professor Oettingen&#x27;s experiments show that optimistic fantasy doesn&#x27;t fuel success — it paralyzes. The Snake River failure was sealed before ignition. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales Evel Knievel Faces the Abyss Positive attitude Success literature Stunt riding Psychology experiments Engineering failure Risk decisions Positive Mental Attitude Manifesting Control Optimists X2 Skycycle\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-04-cautionary-相信能成-所以从不准备-特技车王差点死在4000英尺峡谷/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b996da73a08744ac-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">40:22</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0904</span></div>\n<h2>Believing He Could, So Never Preparing: How the Stunt King Nearly Died in a 4,000-Foot Canyon</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Stunt rider Knievel treated &quot;positive attitude&quot; as a method: no practice runs, no angle calculations, no risk assessment before a jump. Psychology professor Oettingen&#x27;s experiments show that optimistic fantasy doesn&#x27;t fuel success — it paralyzes. The Snake River failure was sealed before ignition.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Positive attitude</span><span class=\"tag\">Success literature</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI Giants Get 80% of Enterprise Revenue From 1% of Customers, Most of Them Living on VC OpenAI and Anthropic get 80% of their enterprise revenue from 1% of customers — and many of those customers are AI companies burning VC-subsidised tokens. The only ones willing to pay real money are tech itself; when VC funding stops, the trillion-dollar compute bill blows up first. Better Offline Better Offline Monologue: Concentration Risk Concentration risk AI bubble Compute contracts OpenAI NVIDIA Venture capital concentration risk take-or-pay agreement neocloud revenue backlog\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-04-betteroffline-ai-巨头-80-企业收入来自-1-客户-多数靠-vc-续命/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fd2855e350ec8287-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"B\"><span class=\"dur\">10:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Better Offline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0904</span></div>\n<h2>AI Giants Get 80% of Enterprise Revenue From 1% of Customers, Most of Them Living on VC</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI and Anthropic get 80% of their enterprise revenue from 1% of customers — and many of those customers are AI companies burning VC-subsidised tokens. The only ones willing to pay real money are tech itself; when VC funding stops, the trillion-dollar compute bill blows up first.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Concentration risk</span><span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI Designing Chips Is Real; Verification Is Still the Number One Bottleneck AI can already write RTL on its own, but the real chokepoint in the entire chip pipeline is verification: it eats more than half of development time, and AI still cannot answer &quot;what should be tested.&quot; OpenAI&#x27;s twenty-person team can shorten the front end, but the back end still has to be left to humans. Asianometry Asianometry AI EDAs: Is It Real? AI chip design EDA Verification OpenAI Agents Semiconductors EDA / Electronic Design Automation RTL / Register Transfer Level PDK / Process Design Kit PPA / Power, Performance, Area tapeout\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-asianometry-ai-设计芯片是真的-验证仍是头号瓶颈/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d3ecab66be5c5d83-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>AI Designing Chips Is Real; Verification Is Still the Number One Bottleneck</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI can already write RTL on its own, but the real chokepoint in the entire chip pipeline is verification: it eats more than half of development time, and AI still cannot answer &quot;what should be tested.&quot; OpenAI&#x27;s twenty-person team can shorten the front end, but the back end still has to be left to humans.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI chip design</span><span class=\"tag\">EDA</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Microsoft&#x27;s Ex-CEO Tried to Route Around the NBA Salary Cap — and Lost: A Star Got $48M for Doing Nothing What really sinks Steve Ballmer isn&#x27;t the $48 million funneled to Kawhi — it&#x27;s that the money bought no real deliverables. The ‘paid for nothing’ clause is what makes the so-called endorsements collapse under investigation. TBPN TBPN Pablo Torre Explains the Steve Ballmer &amp; Kawhi Leonard Scandal NBA Salary Cap Sports Business Financial Investigation Billionaires Sham Contracts salary cap jersey patch sponsor SPAC carbon credits\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-tbpn-微软前ceo绕开nba工资帽的败笔-球星白拿4800万不干活/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c1929723d7b47586-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">23:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">TBPN</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>Microsoft&#x27;s Ex-CEO Tried to Route Around the NBA Salary Cap — and Lost: A Star Got $48M for Doing Nothing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What really sinks Steve Ballmer isn&#x27;t the $48 million funneled to Kawhi — it&#x27;s that the money bought no real deliverables. The ‘paid for nothing’ clause is what makes the so-called endorsements collapse under investigation.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">NBA</span><span class=\"tag\">Salary Cap</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"When Does the AI Bubble Pop? Watch Credit Default Swaps and Token Prices The AI bubble will eventually burst, but current valuations are far below dot-com levels — Nvidia trades at just 15x earnings. The real risk sits in credit markets, where credit default swaps have climbed to historic highs, signalling a possible sharp selloff ahead. Excess Returns Excess Returns Bearish Into November. Room to Run After: Why Dan Niles Is Watching Hyperscaler Credit Default Swaps AI bubble Semiconductors Credit markets Investment strategy Tech stocks Credit Default Swap (CDS) Hyperscaler Token Agentic AI\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-excessreturns-ai泡沫何时破-紧盯信用违约互换与token价格/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3cac5e72b6049e76-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:00:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Excess Returns</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>When Does the AI Bubble Pop? Watch Credit Default Swaps and Token Prices</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The AI bubble will eventually burst, but current valuations are far below dot-com levels — Nvidia trades at just 15x earnings. The real risk sits in credit markets, where credit default swaps have climbed to historic highs, signalling a possible sharp selloff ahead.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span><span class=\"tag\">Semiconductors</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI detection isn&#x27;t about style, it&#x27;s about whether the information is watered down The tell for AI writing isn&#x27;t style — it&#x27;s the &quot;information inflation&quot; of output exceeding input. A hedge-fund titan&#x27;s AI-written op-ed and his public admission became the turning point — Pangram&#x27;s fourth generation has a false-positive rate of about 1 in 24,000, and the more models converge, the easier they are to catch. Oxide and Friends Oxide and Friends AI Detection with Max Spero AI detection content authenticity post-training education anti-cheating marketing astroturf synthetic mirroring humanizer classifier head WildChat\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-oxide-ai-检测不是查文风-是查信息有没有注水/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3e86858ac01c0a5f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">1:01:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Oxide and Friends</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>AI detection isn&#x27;t about style, it&#x27;s about whether the information is watered down</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The tell for AI writing isn&#x27;t style — it&#x27;s the &quot;information inflation&quot; of output exceeding input. A hedge-fund titan&#x27;s AI-written op-ed and his public admission became the turning point — Pangram&#x27;s fourth generation has a false-positive rate of about 1 in 24,000, and the more models converge, the easier they are to catch.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI detection</span><span class=\"tag\">content authenticity</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Ukraine&#x27;s Largest Drone Maker: Nearly 100,000 a Month, and AI Interception Is Just Step One Ukraine&#x27;s General Cherry produces nearly 100,000 drones a month, including interceptors that take down Russian Shaheds costing over $50,000 for about $2,000 each. AI guidance is already in combat, but full autonomy is still far off. Eye On A.I. Eye On A.I. From 10 Drones a Month to Nearly 100,000 — Inside Ukraine&#x27;s Largest Drone Manufacturer | Marko Kushnir, General Cherry Drones AI Ukraine Russia Military Tech Shahed FPV Interceptor drone Moniya\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-eyeonai-乌克兰最大无人机商-月产近10万架-ai拦截是第一步/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/6080df200909c386-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">38:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Eye On A.I.</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>Ukraine&#x27;s Largest Drone Maker: Nearly 100,000 a Month, and AI Interception Is Just Step One</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Ukraine&#x27;s General Cherry produces nearly 100,000 drones a month, including interceptors that take down Russian Shaheds costing over $50,000 for about $2,000 each. AI guidance is already in combat, but full autonomy is still far off.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Drones</span><span class=\"tag\">AI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The Wow! Signal Hasn&#x27;t Been Settled in Nearly 50 Years: It Looks Like an Alien Call, but No Second One Ever Came That 72-second narrowband hydrogen-line signal from 1977 has never repeated, and it falls short of the threshold for evidence of an alien civilization; its legacy isn&#x27;t an answer but a reminder that in a noisy universe, the distance between detection and proof is an entire galaxy. IsaacArthur IsaacArthur The Wow! Signal: Alien Message, Cosmic Fluke, or SETI’s Best False Alarm? Radio Astronomy SETI Alien Signals Scientific Evidence Wow! Signal Astronomy Communication transit telescope hydrogen line water hole maser side lobe technosignature\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-isaacarthur-wow信号近50年没落定-它像外星呼叫-却再没来第二声/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/5655ebd36cb58413-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">35:03</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">IsaacArthur</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>The Wow! Signal Hasn&#x27;t Been Settled in Nearly 50 Years: It Looks Like an Alien Call, but No Second One Ever Came</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">That 72-second narrowband hydrogen-line signal from 1977 has never repeated, and it falls short of the threshold for evidence of an alien civilization; its legacy isn&#x27;t an answer but a reminder that in a noisy universe, the distance between detection and proof is an entire galaxy.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Radio Astronomy</span><span class=\"tag\">SETI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Land Is Not a Commodity: Why a Land Value Tax Can Cure the Housing Crisis The housing shortage is only a symptom; the real disease is land monopoly. A land value tax shifts the burden off buildings and onto land, forcing hoarders to develop or sell, and returning location value to society instead of fattening landlords. MoneyMacro MoneyMacro Can a land value tax fix housing? | Lars Doucet Land Value Tax Housing Crisis Henry George Urban Economics Policy Experiments Land Value Tax (LVT) Georgism YIMBY Mass Appraisal Single Tax Natural Dividend\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-moneymacro-土地不是商品-地价税为何能根治住房危机/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/125e287967146306-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"M\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">MoneyMacro</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>Land Is Not a Commodity: Why a Land Value Tax Can Cure the Housing Crisis</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The housing shortage is only a symptom; the real disease is land monopoly. A land value tax shifts the burden off buildings and onto land, forcing hoarders to develop or sell, and returning location value to society instead of fattening landlords.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Land Value Tax</span><span class=\"tag\">Housing Crisis</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"What Drives Founders Isn&#x27;t Becoming a Billionaire, It&#x27;s the Fear of the Server Crashing at 3 A.M. Most people assume it&#x27;s wealth ambition that carries founders through. Paul Graham says what actually pushes people forward day to day is disaster fear — the server goes down, the model train is about to fall off the table; you keep your head down for ten years, look up, do the math, and realize that at the last round&#x27;s valuation you&#x27;re already a billionaire. Y Combinator Y Combinator Paul Graham On Startups, Ambition, and Great Founders Startup methodology Founder traits YC AGI Inference cost formidable frighteningly ambitious jagged frontier founder mode YC GDP\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-ycsp-驱动创始人的不是当亿万富翁-是怕服务器半夜崩掉/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/516c0e86f9dca57d-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">21:25</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Y Combinator</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>What Drives Founders Isn&#x27;t Becoming a Billionaire, It&#x27;s the Fear of the Server Crashing at 3 A.M.</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Most people assume it&#x27;s wealth ambition that carries founders through. Paul Graham says what actually pushes people forward day to day is disaster fear — the server goes down, the model train is about to fall off the table; you keep your head down for ten years, look up, do the math, and realize that at the last round&#x27;s valuation you&#x27;re already a billionaire.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Startup methodology</span><span class=\"tag\">Founder traits</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Arm Moves Into Building CPUs: The Biggest Bottleneck in Chip Design Is Verification, Not Design The real time sink in a chip cycle is verification, debug and documentation, not RTL; 80%-90% of Arm engineers already use AI daily, and Arm is breaking its 98.5%-gross-margin licensing model to build CPUs itself. No Priors No Priors Redefining Chip Architecture with Arm CEO Rene Haas Arm Chip Design AI Infrastructure SoftBank Supply Chain Robotics IP licensing compute subsystem RTL GDSII\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-nopriors-arm-下场造-cpu-芯片设计最大瓶颈是验证-不是设计/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e36b80375fbfde6c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">37:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">No Priors</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>Arm Moves Into Building CPUs: The Biggest Bottleneck in Chip Design Is Verification, Not Design</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The real time sink in a chip cycle is verification, debug and documentation, not RTL; 80%-90% of Arm engineers already use AI daily, and Arm is breaking its 98.5%-gross-margin licensing model to build CPUs itself.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Arm</span><span class=\"tag\">Chip Design</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Number One Fraud Red Flag Isn&#x27;t Greed — It&#x27;s Personal Finances Already Out of Control For 14 straight years, ACFE has ranked &quot;personal financial problems&quot; as the top red flag for financial misconduct; systemic incentives, a critical brain region going offline, and moral overconfidence all let good people cross the line step by step. The Rational Reminder Podcast Rational Reminder The Ethics Problem in Financial Services (Dr. Moira Somers &amp; Philippa Hann) | Rational Reminder 425 Financial ethics Financial advisers Investor protection Fraud red flags Behavioral finance CFP ACFE / Association of Certified Fraud Examiners CFP / Certified Financial Planner\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-rationalreminder-金融舞弊头号预警-不是贪婪-是个人财务先失控/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2de1b986a9bfa34c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:40:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">The Rational Reminder Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>The Number One Fraud Red Flag Isn&#x27;t Greed — It&#x27;s Personal Finances Already Out of Control</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">For 14 straight years, ACFE has ranked &quot;personal financial problems&quot; as the top red flag for financial misconduct; systemic incentives, a critical brain region going offline, and moral overconfidence all let good people cross the line step by step.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Financial ethics</span><span class=\"tag\">Financial advisers</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The 5% Treasury Yield Isn&#x27;t About Inflation: $32 Trillion of Debt Means Buyers Will Only Take More Inflation can&#x27;t explain a 30-year above 5%: even with no inflation and no default risk, a buyer already full up on Treasuries at 5.3% won&#x27;t budge for another $10 billion. What&#x27;s really steepening the curve is $2 trillion of new supply a year, and the Treasury can&#x27;t hold it down with buybacks. Odd Lots Odd Lots What&#x27;s Behind the Big Surge in US Government Bond Yields Treasury yields Buybacks Federal Reserve Fiscal dominance Jackson Hole term premium fiscal dominance off-the-run Treasuries ratchet effect Treasury General Account (TGA)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-oddlots-美债利率上-5-不是通胀闹的-32-万亿国债让买家只肯加价接盘/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">36:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>The 5% Treasury Yield Isn&#x27;t About Inflation: $32 Trillion of Debt Means Buyers Will Only Take More</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Inflation can&#x27;t explain a 30-year above 5%: even with no inflation and no default risk, a buyer already full up on Treasuries at 5.3% won&#x27;t budge for another $10 billion. What&#x27;s really steepening the curve is $2 trillion of new supply a year, and the Treasury can&#x27;t hold it down with buybacks.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasury yields</span><span class=\"tag\">Buybacks</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"A wallet&#x27;s profit engine isn&#x27;t interest on balances, it&#x27;s money moving inside the system The core ledger of a wallet: money coming in pays card-network tolls, internal transfers cost almost nothing, and money going out can be charged again. It earns the spread on flow, not interest on deposits — PayPal, Cash App and Stripe Link are all betting on this model. Complex Systems Complex Systems Everyone wants to be your wallet Payments Wallets Card networks Stripe Fintech ACH interchange Durbin-exempt institution bps\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-complexsys-钱包的利润密码不是余额利息-是钱在体系内流转/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/939355004e704d04-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">33:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Complex Systems</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>A wallet&#x27;s profit engine isn&#x27;t interest on balances, it&#x27;s money moving inside the system</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The core ledger of a wallet: money coming in pays card-network tolls, internal transfers cost almost nothing, and money going out can be charged again. It earns the spread on flow, not interest on deposits — PayPal, Cash App and Stripe Link are all betting on this model.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Payments</span><span class=\"tag\">Wallets</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"If It Can&#x27;t Solve Quantum Gravity, It Isn&#x27;t Real AGI A physicist draws a high line for AGI: solving quantum gravity is the bar. The conversation also clarifies the real relationship between quantum materials and AI — searched-for materials still have to pass the synthesizability gate, and the result may be zero. South Park Commons South Park Commons I’ll Believe in AGI When It Solves Quantum Gravity | Prof. Rajesh Gopakumar | Theoretical Physicist AGI String Theory Quantum Materials AI for Science Talent Density Science Funding Quantum gravity String theory Bose-Einstein condensation Synthesizability\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-spc-解不出量子引力-就不算真正的-agi/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/00b7c1ae9f5f7539-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:28:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">South Park Commons</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>If It Can&#x27;t Solve Quantum Gravity, It Isn&#x27;t Real AGI</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A physicist draws a high line for AGI: solving quantum gravity is the bar. The conversation also clarifies the real relationship between quantum materials and AI — searched-for materials still have to pass the synthesizability gate, and the result may be zero.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AGI</span><span class=\"tag\">String Theory</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s front-runners are just oil refineries, not the native-app winners AI has entered its agent phase: the first-stage leaders are only refineries, not the native-app winners; new platforms don&#x27;t come from old platforms; organizations must move from jobs to tasks; and in the end what people compete on is the creativity to conjure something from nothing. 张小珲·商业访谈录 张小珲·商业访谈录 153. 和曾鸣聊产业史观：残酷的真相、会消亡的公司、优秀≠卓越、“OAI、Anth大概率不是原生时代大赢家” AI industry Strategy methodology Organizational change Agents Corporate death Incumbent transition Token factory Agentic OS New Lab High agency Context not control\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-03-zhangxiaojun-ai没有安全巨头-公司制度将消亡/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2be28ff846f98de7-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"张\"><span class=\"dur\">2:34:18</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">张小珲·商业访谈录</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0903</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s front-runners are just oil refineries, not the native-app winners</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI has entered its agent phase: the first-stage leaders are only refineries, not the native-app winners; new platforms don&#x27;t come from old platforms; organizations must move from jobs to tasks; and in the end what people compete on is the creativity to conjure something from nothing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI industry</span><span class=\"tag\">Strategy methodology</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI writing&#x27;s moat isn&#x27;t the model, it&#x27;s the proprietary data you feed it Every writer Katie spent two years turning ChatGPT from a career coach during a layoff into a one-person content company and a compounding editor; the core method isn&#x27;t prompts, it&#x27;s using proprietary experience to cover the &quot;last mile&quot; the model can&#x27;t reach. AI &amp; I AI &amp; I（Every） How a Professional Writer Writes With AI AI writing context engineering compound feedback Codex content entrepreneurship AI and mental health context engineering last mile problem compound engineering computer errands\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-02-aiandi-ai-写作的护城河不是模型-而是你喂进去的独家数据/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d5ef936d3e5abbde-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">47:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">AI &amp; I</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0902</span></div>\n<h2>AI writing&#x27;s moat isn&#x27;t the model, it&#x27;s the proprietary data you feed it</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Every writer Katie spent two years turning ChatGPT from a career coach during a layoff into a one-person content company and a compounding editor; the core method isn&#x27;t prompts, it&#x27;s using proprietary experience to cover the &quot;last mile&quot; the model can&#x27;t reach.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI writing</span><span class=\"tag\">context engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Stronger Models Make Dirty Data Deadlier: Cleaning Is Worth More, Not Less Jane Street&#x27;s alternative data team found that once data leaks future information into the past, the stronger the model, the more dangerous it gets; pinning down &quot;what was known at the time&quot; is worth more than tuning the model. Signals and Threads Signals and Threads Wrestling the world into rows with Eric Mannes Alternative Data Data Engineering Quant Trading Jane Street Data Quality Cost Models alt data anti-inductive environment point-in-time data desk dev\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-02-signalsandthre-模型越强-脏数据越致命-清洗反而更值钱/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e531b327a316d7bc-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:25:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Signals and Threads</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0902</span></div>\n<h2>Stronger Models Make Dirty Data Deadlier: Cleaning Is Worth More, Not Less</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Jane Street&#x27;s alternative data team found that once data leaks future information into the past, the stronger the model, the more dangerous it gets; pinning down &quot;what was known at the time&quot; is worth more than tuning the model.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Alternative Data</span><span class=\"tag\">Data Engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The most valuable step in writing with AI isn&#x27;t the prompt — it&#x27;s compounding your revision feedback Katie took AI from professional coach all the way to writing plugin: first load the model with context, then store every revision note back into the system and let it compound. For her, AI&#x27;s value isn&#x27;t just speed — it&#x27;s a support system that steadies her and gets her past execution hurdles. Every Every How a Professional Writer Writes With AI Writing AI Workflow Context Engineering Feedback Compounding Career Coaching Agent Compound Engineering Compound Writing context engineering supportive technology MCP\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-09-02-every-用-ai-写作最值钱的一步不是提示词-而是把改稿反馈沉淀成复利/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8c7062f58fa066c8-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">48:26</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Every</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0902</span></div>\n<h2>The most valuable step in writing with AI isn&#x27;t the prompt — it&#x27;s compounding your revision feedback</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Katie took AI from professional coach all the way to writing plugin: first load the model with context, then store every revision note back into the system and let it compound. For her, AI&#x27;s value isn&#x27;t just speed — it&#x27;s a support system that steadies her and gets her past execution hurdles.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Writing</span><span class=\"tag\">AI Workflow</span>\n</div></div></a>"]